From 34fb547fb49397ee1ff1b95aedb98649f20c79c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:41:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] e-acsl-gcc: compile with -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE, as
 Frama-C preprocesses

e-acsl-gcc preprocesses the sources for Frama-C with
"-std=c99 -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE" (FRAMAC_CPP_EXTRA), but compiles both the
original and the instrumented program with "-std=c99" alone (CFLAGS).
With glibc, -std=c99 alone hides the POSIX and BSD declarations
(strdup, stpcpy, strtok_r, fileno, getline, ...): Frama-C sees and
instruments the calls, while the compiler sees implicit int
declarations. GCC 14 rejects the resulting int-to-pointer conversion,
so any program calling such a function fails to build
("fail to compile/link un-instrumented code"; with -L, the instrumented
code, which includes the libc headers, fails the same way).

Add -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE next to -std=c99 in CFLAGS, so that the compiler
sees the same declarations as Frama-C. -std=c99 itself is unchanged.

Test: libc/default_source.c calls stpcpy. Its dev run uses -L, since
the test configuration always passes -X and so never compiles the
original program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
